Z||000000||thecage||10-22-2001||09:43 PM||||Here's my problem. The car starts up real quick first shot no problem. When I drive the car for awhile operating temperature and go to start it up it takes 4-5 sec. of cranking to get it to start. The car has to sit for approx. 1 hour or more to get it to start up instantly. The funny twist to this is after it is hot and it took a few seconds to start if i shut the car off and restart it right away it starts instantly. Any direction to this problem would be helpful. I've also noticed that when I shut the car off I do not get any smell of gasoline but when I go start it after it is hot and it takes a few seconds to start I do get some smell of gasoline. Any help would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gary W||10-22-2001||09:48 PM||||If it's a V6<BR>Could be the pickup coil in the distributor or the ignition module. They tend to fail when hot. If it starts cold, it's not the fuel pump relay. <p>[This message has been edited by Gary W (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||thecage||10-22-2001||10:17 PM||||Any way of testing the ignition module or the distributor coil||||reg||1
Z||000003||thecage||10-26-2001||08:47 PM||||Sorry for the delay in time but I drive the car once in awhile, (it's a toy). I have bought a fuel pump relay, pick up coil, ingnition module and ignition coil. I have not installed any of these things in the car yet (86 GT, 4spd). Before I do can my problem be related to a bad ground somewhere. The only reason I say this is my radio always looses it's programmed stations once i shut the car off, could there be any relation to my starting problems when hot due to this. Like I said before it cranks and start's ok just takes a few seconds before engine catches unlike first time i start it cold instant start. I only drive the car once a week or two weeks so finding the solution is a slow process. I just bought the car 2months ago and I'm slowly working on to get it ready to be my daily driver in the spring and summer.<BR>Your help is most appreciated.<BR>Anyone know where I can get a center console dark grey mine has a large crack in it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gary W||10-26-2001||09:30 PM||||Take off the distributor cap and look at the pickup coil. In many cases, they just melt or corrode into a green mess. Since you already have the parts, you might as well do the ignition tune-up and eliminate those parts. A bad ground would probably keep the engine from cranking, but it wouldn't hurt to check all the connections on both ends of both battery cables.||||reg||1
Z||000005||thecage||10-26-2001||09:53 PM||||thanks gary w for the info. so since my cranking of the engine is fine I can say that the grounding does not affect the starting problem. Also how long would it take for the engine bay to cool. I drove it today a couple of miles maybe 3, let it stand for about 1 1/2 hours and went to restart still had that problem. But when I started the car this morning before my trip (had not drove it since last Sunday) she fired up instantly. Very annoying problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTZ34||10-27-2001||12:58 PM||||Cage, A shot in the dark here but...  Verify that when you start the car cold, that the fuel pump is being turned on.  Do this by putting the key in the on position.  It sounds like it is but check anyway.  You should hear a low pump noise. After you run the car and its warm, do the same test but leave the key off for about 15 seconds (about double the off time to reset the pump timer) after you shut it down. My theory is that the fuel pump relay is being affected by heat meaning that is works when cold, but when hot the back-up mechanism is being used.  The fuel system back-up mechanism is triggered by oil pressure and it will turn on the fuel pump when min pressure is reached which also turns off the oil light.<P>Opps - didn't see the part about the fuel smell but this test will verify the fuel pump electrical circuit anyway.  Most likely you have injector or ignition problems causing the fuel smell while starting hot.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||thecage||10-27-2001||10:17 PM||||Thank's all for the info. i'm going to replace one item at a time and test the result's so i know exactly what it was that caused the problem. I will keep you posted as to the results. I'm going to lick this problem yet.||||reg||1
